/**
 * German for the Vivere in Italia practice questions.
 *
 * The lessons of this course have read in German since the Italian table was
 * written; the practice bank behind them had none, so the practice tab and
 * the exam went on asking in Italian. The fourth of the seven banks.
 *
 * Keyed on the ITALIAN of itQuestionBank.ts, exactly as it stands there. Every
 * key was extracted from the built module and paired back by position, never
 * retyped: one wrong character — a grave accent for an acute, an apostrophe of
 * the wrong kind — and the lookup misses in silence, so the marker disappears
 * and the reader is told there is nothing for a question that was in fact
 * translated.
 *
 * Names of offices, laws and dishes stay Italian, as they do in
 * VIVERE_IN_ITALIA_DE: codice fiscale, Ferragosto, aperitivo, caffè corretto,
 * primo and secondo. That is what the exam asks for. What is translated is the
 * explanation around them. One question is about the four A of Italian export
 * — abbigliamento, automazione, arredamento, alimentare — where all four
 * options begin with A in Italian: translating the words alone would take the
 * question apart, so they keep the Italian with a German gloss beside it.
 *
 * Strings another German table already answers are deliberately absent. Every
 * table for one target is spread into a single object, so a second entry for
 * the same key would be a silent collision, and the older table would decide
 * the wording for both. check-question-bank-translation counts what a reader
 * reaches rather than what this file holds.
 */
